    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0174_a0780233a833.png\" style=\"width: 113px; height: 116px;\" /></p><p>Intramolecular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonding</p><p>thus it is more volatile due to intramolecular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonding.</p><p>Melting point of o-nitrophenol is higher because of closed packing and not because of hydrogen bonding.</p>"
